Bug: Expiry check use `<` (less-than) not `<=` (less-than-or-equal). When current time equals expiry time, `<` evaluates false, token rejected when still valid.

**Fix:**
```javascript
// Buggy
if (currentTime < expiryTime) { /* valid */ }

// Fixed
if (currentTime <= expiryTime) { /* valid */ }
```

Or inverse:
```javascript
// Buggy
if (expiryTime <= currentTime) { reject(); }

// Fixed  
if (expiryTime < currentTime) { reject(); }
```

