In React, inline objects are created anew on every render with different memory references. React uses shallow equality to detect prop changes, so a new object reference triggers a child re-render even if values are identical.

One concrete fix is to use `useMemo` to memoize the object:

```jsx
import { useMemo } from 'react'

function Parent() {
  const config = useMemo(() => ({ name: 'John' }), [])
  return <Child config={config} />
}
```

This ensures the same object reference persists across renders, preventing unnecessary child re-renders.

