React re-renders a child component when its parent passes an inline object prop because a new object reference is created on every render. React compares props by reference equality (===), so the child detects a "new" prop value even if the content is identical.

**Concrete fix: Use `useMemo` to memoize the object:**

```jsx
import { useMemo } from 'react';

function Parent() {
  const config = useMemo(() => ({ theme: 'dark' }), []);
  return <Child config={config} />;
}
```

This ensures the same object reference is reused across renders, preventing unnecessary child re-renders.
